---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CTABanner from '../../components/CTABanner.astro';
import PageBanner from '../../components/PageBanner.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
import { reviews } from '../../data/reviews';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'About', path: '/about' },
  { name: 'What to Expect', path: '/what-to-expect' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What to Expect When You Hire Us | Austin Tree Care"
  description="Free estimates, on-site arborist visits, scheduling, payment, and storm triage: how hiring Blue Ox Tree Care works in Austin. Call (512) 749-8615."
  schema={breadcrumbSchema(breadcrumbs)}
>
  <PageBanner
    title="What to Expect"
    description="Here is how working with Blue Ox Tree Care goes, from your first call until the job is done."
    breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  />

  <section class="py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4">
      <div class="space-y-12 text-ox-navy/90">
        <div>
          <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-ox-navy">How the free estimate works</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Start by calling {site.phone} or sending a message through our{' '}
            <a href={withBase('/contact')} class="link-body">contact page</a>. Tell us about your trees,
            where you live, and what you need. That could be trimming, removal, a sick tree, storm
            damage, or a general checkup. We set up a visit at a time that works for you.
          </p>
          <p>
            Estimates are free for most jobs. A certified arborist meets you at your home. You won't
            get a salesperson reading from a script. Travis Berlin (ISA BCMA, RM-7612B) or Lacy Berlin
            (ISA Certified Arborist, RM-8632A) looks at your trees and talks through your choices. Then
            you get a written estimate with the work and the price before any work starts.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-ox-navy">The visit to your home</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            During the visit, we look at what kind of trees you have, how strong they are, how healthy
            they are, and what needs clearing. We also check for any rules that apply, like City of
            Austin protected tree rules, oak wilt risk, or HOA rules. We look from the ground and use
            our training. If you need a{' '}
            <a href={withBase('/services/tree-risk-assessment')} class="link-body">formal risk check</a>,
            we have special tools for that.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="check-mark mt-1">✓</span>
              Please make sure we can get through your gate, and mark any buried lines or sprinklers you know about
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="check-mark mt-1">✓</span>
              Please keep pets inside and the driveway clear so we can work safely
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="check-mark mt-1">✓</span>
              Tell us about any neighbor or HOA concerns. We can plan for trees on a shared property line
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-ox-navy">When we can do the work</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            We usually schedule routine pruning and tree health work within one to three weeks after
            you say yes. It depends on the season and how busy our crew is. Storm damage and dangerous
            trees come first. We handle safety threats first, then schedule any follow-up work.
          </p>
          <p>
            Oak wilt is a disease that kills oaks. It can affect when it is safe to prune live oaks
            if the work can wait. Our{' '}
            <a href={withBase('/guides/oak-wilt-austin')} class="link-body">oak wilt guide</a> explains
            the best and worst times of year. During your estimate, we tell you the best time for your
            trees.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-ox-navy">Payment</h2>
          <p>
            Your estimate lists the payment terms. We take the usual forms of payment, and we can talk
            about billing for larger jobs. There are no hidden fees. Haul-away, stump grinding, and
            permit help (when needed) are listed up front. You know the full job before work starts.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-ox-navy">Where we work</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            We serve the Austin area. That includes central and west Austin neighborhoods with big old
            trees, plus West Lake Hills, Barton Creek, Circle C, Steiner Ranch, and other towns within
            about 50 miles of central Austin. See our{' '}
            <a href={withBase('/neighborhoods')} class="link-body">neighborhood tree care pages</a> for
            tips about your area.
          </p>
          <p>
            We have no storefront or street address to visit. We come to your home.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-ox-navy">After a storm</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            After bad weather, call {site.phone} if you have hanging branches, split trunks, or trees
            that could fall on a building. We make the dangers safe first. Then we plan the full
            cleanup. Read our{' '}
            <a href={withBase('/journal/central-texas-storm-tree-triage')} class="link-body">storm checklist</a>{' '}
            for safety steps to take before we get there.
          </p>
          <p>
            For emergency storm work, see our{' '}
            <a href={withBase('/services/storm-damage')} class="link-body">storm damage service</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="callout-panel">
          <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-ox-navy">Credentials you can verify</h2>
          <p class="mb-4 text-sm text-ox-navy/80">
            Travis Berlin is an ISA Board Certified Master Arborist (RM-7612B). Fewer than 2% of ISA
            Certified Arborists earn this title. Lacy Berlin is an ISA Certified Arborist (RM-8632A).
            We are licensed and insured for dangerous tree work. You can check both credentials at
            isa-arbor.com.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
            <li>
              <a href={withBase('/arborists/travis-berlin')} class="link-aside font-medium">Travis Berlin →</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href={withBase('/arborists/lacy-berlin')} class="link-aside font-medium">Lacy Berlin →</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href={withBase('/journal/hiring-isa-arborist-austin-bcma')} class="link-aside font-medium">What BCMA means →</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ox-navy/80">
            {reviews.rating.toFixed(1)} stars · {reviews.count} Google reviews.{' '}
            <a href={site.googleProfile} class="link-body" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              Read reviews
            </a>
            {' · '}
            <a href={site.googleWriteReview} class="link-body" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              Write a review
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABanner heading="Ready to get started?" subtext="Call or send a request for a free estimate. We serve the Austin area and come to you." />
</BaseLayout>
